<title>SWITZERLAND: Clariant H1 sales rise 12 pct.</title>
<headline>Clariant H1 sales rise 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MUTTENZ, Switzerland 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30, 1997</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group sales		    1,415	     vs 1,139</p>
<p>Sales by product</p>
<p> Textile dyes		   389		 vs 329</p>
<p> Textile chemicals	    215		 vs 170</p>
<p> Leather			  143		 vs 115</p>
<p> Paper			    201		 vs 157</p>
<p> Pigments/Additives	   156		 vs 132</p>
<p> Masterbatches		  263		 vs 188</p>
<p> Other			    48		  vs 48</p>
<p>Note - Full name of Swiss specialty chemicals producer is Clariant AG.</p>
<p>Total sales were 12 percent higher in local currencies and 24 percent higher on a Swiss franc basis.</p>
<p>Clariant said 38 million francs of the sales attributed to Masterbatches was due to acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
